  "methods_narrative": "HuBMAP lung snRNA-seq nuclei were loaded from Salmon-processed `raw_expr.h5ad` (scanpy 1.11.5, anndata 0.12.19). QC used scanpy.pp.calculate_qc_metrics for gene counts, UMI totals, and mitochondrial/ribosomal percentages, then filtered to min_genes=200, min_counts=500, max_mito_percent=5.0, max_genes=8000, and genes in >=3 nuclei. Doublet detection was not applied in the core teaching path. Counts were library-size normalized (target_sum=10000) and log1p-transformed with raw counts retained in `.layers['counts']`. Highly variable genes (Seurat flavor, n=2000) were scaled (clip=10) and embedded with PCA (50 components, arpack). A kNN graph (n_neighbors=15) and UMAP (min_dist=0.3, spread=1.0) were computed for visualization.",
